      "latin": "Pater digitō silentium suāsit. Theodōrus, quī alibī clāmāre solet, hīc vōce summissā «Pluteī sunt, tata,» inquit, «sīcut avī, sed aurātī.»",
      "english": "Dad put a finger to his lips. Theo, who shouts everywhere else, said here in a low voice, “They’re bookshelves, Dad, like Grandpa’s, but golden.”",
